### Status Card

Create one minimal dark rounded status card containing exactly two rows.

#### Month Row

Render:

- small calendar outline icon using the accent color
- text exactly: `{{ challenge.month_label }}`

Emphasize the current month number using the accent color.

Render the total number with lower visual emphasis or reduced opacity.

#### MRR Row

Below one thin divider, render:

- small coin or currency outline icon
- text exactly: `Current MRR: {{ content.revenue_label }}`

Emphasize `{{ content.revenue_label }}` using the accent color.

Do NOT add any other information inside this card.

Specifically, do not add:

- start date
- deadline
- calendar month name
- current-period labels
- progress percentage
- target MRR
- secondary statistics

### Progress Bar

Render one long horizontal progress bar.

Start label:

`{{ challenge.start_mrr_formatted }}`

End label:

`{{ challenge.target_mrr_formatted }}`

Progress label:

`{{ revenue.target_progress_percent }}%`

The visual fill length and circular marker position must correspond to exactly {{ revenue.target_progress_percent }}% of the distance from the starting value to the target value.

Place the percentage near the progress marker so it clearly belongs to that position.

When progress is very small, keep the percentage readable and clear of the start label.

Never center the percentage on the full track unless the actual progress position requires it.

Do not draw any revenue history chart.

## Composition

You have full freedom to place every required element anywhere on the canvas, subject only to:

1. the canvas safe margins
2. the bottom-left content exclusion zone
{% if watermark.enabled %}
3. the attribution reservation (see below)
{% endif %}

Do not force a fixed left/right/bottom region split. Choose a composition that feels balanced for a wide 3:1 banner.

Still include every Visible Content element exactly once.

### Visual Hierarchy

Use approximately this visual hierarchy (relative size/weight — not placement):

- top label: small
- headline: very large, bold, condensed or semi-condensed
- subtitle: medium
- apps section label: small to medium
- app information: compact
- status card: secondary to the headline; do not make it oversized

The headline should visually dominate all other elements.

Use generous negative space around the headline.

Do not turn the banner into a dense dashboard.

{% if apps %}

### App Block Structure

Preferred visual structure for each app:

`[APP ICON]  App Name    $X.XX MRR`

Underneath:

`[Store icon] amount   |   [Store icon] amount`

Do not put individual apps inside separate large cards.

{% endif %}

### Progress Bar Presentation

The progress bar should:

- remain visually simple
- have comfortable padding around it and its labels
- keep all of its labels, fill, and marker clear of the bottom-left exclusion zone
