{% endif %}

## Progress Bar Style

Use:

- capsule or pill-shaped track
- rounded ends
- dark translucent track
- subtle low-contrast border
- filled section using a smooth accent-to-primary gradient
- circular marker at the fill edge
- thin light outline around the marker
- optional subtle tick marks

Do not use:

- stacked bars
- line charts
- revenue charts
- legends
- fake data points
- axes

{% if apps %}

## App Icon Chroma Markers

Real app icons will be composited programmatically after generation.

For each app, create exactly one chroma marker.

Marker requirements:

- target size: approximately 48 × 48 px
- acceptable range: 42–52 px
- rounded square
- approximately 12 px corner radius (~25% of marker size; must match post-process mask)
- fill exactly {{ icon_marker_hex }}
- if {{ icon_marker_hex }} is `#FF0000`, use RGB exactly `(255, 0, 0)`
- completely flat solid fill
- no gradient
- no border
- no shadow
- no glow
- no texture
- no icon
- no glyph
- no lettering
- no artwork inside the marker

Keep at least approximately 8 px of non-red space around every marker.

The marker must remain fully visible and unobstructed.

Do not place:

- text over it
- decorative lines over it
- glow over it
- borders over it
- UI elements over it

Pure {{ icon_marker_hex }} must not appear anywhere else in the generated image.

{% endif %}

## Store Icons

App Store and Play Store icons are NOT post-processed.

They must be drawn directly in the generated banner.

For each app:

- draw one small recognizable App Store icon beside the App Store MRR amount
- draw one small recognizable Play Store icon beside the Play Store MRR amount
- target approximately 14–20 px visual size
- keep them clean and immediately recognizable
- use them as compact platform indicators

Do not use chroma markers for store icons.

Do not write the platform names as text.

